  "output": {
    "answer": "The record's answer is the flag, not the gate. A gate only checks the result against a bar decided in advance, so it can pass something wrong in a way that bar didn't cover. What stops that from reaching users is that new behavior ships behind a flag that defaults off in production even after merging — a lane can flip its own dev flag, but only I flip the production flag, explicitly, the next morning, never automatically when a lane finishes. So a bad merge sits inert until I look at it. Beyond that, the record doesn't show additional unanticipated-error catches.",
